Vikram and Betal: The Sharing Child (Raw Story)

id: WBX_100132

King Vikram was carrying Betal through the forest once again.

Betal began his story.

“Once there was a child who loved sweets,” said Betal. “He always kept them to himself.”

One day, his friend came to visit him.

The child had many sweets but did not offer any.

His friend felt sad but said nothing.

Later, the child went to his friend’s house.

This time, the friend happily shared all his sweets.

The child felt ashamed.

He realized that sharing brings happiness.

From that day on, he always shared with others.

Betal then asked, “Vikram, what changed the child?”

Vikram replied, “He learned by seeing kindness.”

As soon as Vikram spoke, Betal flew back to the tree.

💖 Moral:

Sharing brings happiness.
